.TH CJSON_DICTIONARY_NEXT 3 "2026-09-29" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_dictionary_next \- step a dictionary cursor onto the next member
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cjson.h>

bool cjson_dictionary_next(cjson_dictionary_iter *it);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Steps the cursor it, which cjson_dictionary_first(3) filled, onto the
member that follows the current one in insertion order.  After a call
that returns true, it->key and it->value describe that member.
cjson_dictionary_first(3) describes the order, the lifetime of
it->key and the changes that the cursor survives.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
it  A cursor that cjson_dictionary_first(3) filled.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
true when it now stands on the next member.

false when the previous call gave the last member, and on every call
after that.  The function then sets it->key and it->value to NULL.
false also when it is NULL.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The cursor survives the replacement of any value, an insert, and
the removal of any member other than the one that this call is
about to read.  cjson_dictionary_first(3) states the exact rule.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_dictionary_first (3),
.BR cjson_dictionary_remove (3)
